SUMMARY:Deadline: Have your say on advancing AI transparency in Canada
DESCRIPTION:Innovation\, Science and Economic Development Canada\nTwo-month
  consultation under the AI for All strategy on five transparency mechanism
 s: detecting AI-generated content\, disclosing when people interact with A
 I\, standardized information about AI systems\, tracking serious AI incide
 nts\, and tracking the activities of AI agents.\nWhy it matters: It is the
  first federal vehicle for incident reporting and agent-tracking rules sin
 ce AIDA died\, so submissions here shape Canada's baseline transparency re
 gime for frontier models.\nHow to participate: Answer the online questionn
 aire or email a written submission through the ISED consultation page befo
 re 23 September 2026.\nhttps://ised-isde.canada.ca/site/ised/en/have-your-
 say-advancing-ai-transparency-canada\nTracked by AI Consultation Deadlines
  Canada: https://donjguido.github.io/ai-consultation-deadlines-canada
URL:https://ised-isde.canada.ca/site/ised/en/have-your-say-advancing-ai-tra
 nsparency-canada
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
CATEGORIES:frontier-models,deepfakes,standards
